! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! RECORDED AND NOT EXPLAINED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A BARE "*" AFTER THE LOCATION on lines 16, 20, 26 and 46 --
! "216740.40 *", "216743.00 *", "217034.00 *", "217052.40 *".
! printed pp.3, 37, 103, 120, 128 and 136 carry the same mark and it
! was left unexplained on each.  It changes no compiled bit.  Line
! 20 is a DR and line 26 is an entry-mode DD, but lines 21-23 and
! 24-25 are the same two shapes and carry no mark, so it is not a
! marker for either.
!
! >>> THE FOUR RESERVATIONS ARE "DR", NOT "DRZ", AND decks/mcp_
! bootstrap_p136.strap's COMMENT SAYS DRZ. <<<  p.136's header
! quotes the volume OCR as "P TEM BF  DRZ(BU,64),(13)" and
! "P PP BF  DRZ(BU,64),(13)".  Rendered at 1200 dpi, lines 20-23 of
! THIS page print "DR(BU,64),(13)" with no Z -- and the volume OCR
! itself reads "DR(BU,64),(13)" on both rows, so the Z is in p.136's
! comment and not in the ink or in the OCR.  It changes no bit on
! p.136 (which only SYNs the symbols) but it DOES change this page:
! C22-6531 printed p.35 makes DRZ "exactly" a DR whose words "are
! all set to zero", so DRZ would plant 49 words of zero content in
! the merged image where DR plants none.  The deck writes DR, as
! printed.  p.136's comment should be corrected.
!
! LINE 27's CNOP PRINTS NEITHER A LOCATION NOR BINARY OUTPUT, and
! line 19's prints both ("216742.40  000000.30 00").  That is the
! pseudo-op working: P UNNOT's six words end at 217042.00, which is
! already a full-word boundary, so line 27's CNOP has nothing to
! round and emits nothing; line 19 follows a half-word branch at
! 216742.00 and emits the NOP.  C22-6531's "CNOP".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! AGREEMENT WITH THE VOLUME SURVEY
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The survey OCR'd 18 rows carrying a LOCATION, range
! 216734.CC..217047.0C.  THIS READING DISAGREES ON THE COUNT AND ON
! BOTH ENDPOINTS: 41 rows carry a LOCATION, the first is 216731.00
! and the last is 217056.00 -- so the survey read fewer than half of
! them and missed three words at the top and six at the bottom.  Re-run here, strap/mcp_ocr.py reads the same 18 rows
! and every one of them agrees with the reading above; it simply
! drops the other twenty-six.  The survey is a lower bound, as its
! brief says, and the endpoints it reports are the endpoints of what
! it happened to read.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! COVERAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! 33 !CHECK rows and 15 !SYM lines.  The rows with NO !CHECK are:
!   lines 20-23   DR reservations.  The BINARY OUTPUT column prints
!                 the reservation's SIZE (000015.00 = 13 words,
!                 000012.00 = 10) and not its contents, so they get
!                 no !CHECK -- printed pp.42, 84, 109 and 119's
!                 convention.  All four sizes ARE checked, by the
!                 !SYM of the symbol that follows each.
!   lines 24-28   the four entry-mode DDs and the empty CNOP.  The
!                 listing prints no bits for them.  All four DDs'
!                 lengths are checked by the following !SYM.
!   lines 4, 29-37, 47, 52, 53, 55   comment cards.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!SYM   PMPLEV   216732.40
!SYM   GERROR   216733.40
!SYM   GODBOC   216735.00
!SYM   PDBRET   216736.40
!SYM   PTEMBF   216743.00
!SYM   PPPBF    216760.00
!SYM   PMCPBF   216775.00
!SYM   GMISTO   217012.00
!SYM   PEPGK    217024.00
!SYM   PUK      217030.00
!SYM   PUNNOT   217034.00
!SYM   PMSGER   217042.00
!SYM   GEDIT    217045.00
!SYM   GOKOLO   217047.00
!SYM   GKONTR   217055.00
